ALVA — Universal Attack Classification and Absolute Shield Protection

Objective

Inspect the entire Alva repository and implement a permanent, universal combat rule:

Anything whose purpose is to deal damage, or that can directly or indirectly result in damage, must be considered an ATTACK, regardless of its name, animation, ability category, execution mechanism, or character.

This includes techniques, summons, projectiles, special abilities, reflected projectiles, multi-hit abilities, damage-producing effects, and any future mechanics capable of causing damage.

A successfully active Shield must block every attack without exception.

Deflect is a special case: it is simultaneously a defensive ability and an offensive attack.

These rules must apply automatically to every current character and every character added in the future.

Do not solve this problem through hardcoded character IDs, lists of existing move names, or individual exceptions.

