Final acceptance criteria

The implementation is only complete if all these statements are true:

RULE 1: If an action can cause damage, directly or indirectly, it is an attack.

RULE 2: Its name does not determine whether it is an attack.

RULE 3: Summons, techniques, projectiles, and other offensive mechanisms remain attacks even though they have different execution types.

RULE 4: Deflect is both an attack and a defensive action.

RULE 5: Every attack is blockable by an active Shield, without exceptions.

RULE 6: A blocked attack cannot inflict damage, increase Launch Point, or apply offensive hit effects through the Shield.

RULE 7: Existing ability names, controls, animations, and unrelated mechanics remain intact.

RULE 8: All current characters and future characters must follow these rules automatically.

RULE 9: There must be no hidden damage pathway that avoids the universal Shield check.

RULE 10: The rules must be enforced by combat architecture and tests, not merely by documentation.

Guiding principle

An attack is defined by its offensive capability, not by its name or how the game executes it.

A Shield is defined by its ability to block attacks, not by which attacks happen to be allowed through it.

Implement these principles universally and permanently across Alva.
